caption: Closed Intrinsic Trait Universe
engine-rule: closed-intrinsic-trait-universe

The fixed Source must determine a closed universe of legal Atavistic purchases. That universe may be expressed as a fixed trait list, a complete creature or racial template, a Source Profile, a closed category ledger, or an objective rule that determines whether a trait belongs. Ordinary advancement cannot add a trait merely by analogy, theme, visual similarity, folklore association, or GM improvisation.

A legal Atavistic trait must be intrinsic to the Source or be explicitly included by the Tradition's Source rules. Intrinsic traits may include anatomy, physiology, senses, movement, natural weapons, defenses, resistances, recovery, environmental adaptations, inherent supernatural abilities, built-in construct systems, and similar properties of the embodied Source. Learned skills, techniques, spells learned as skills, ordinary equipment, Wealth, Status, Rank, Reputation, cultural knowledge, and other learned, social, or external material do not enter the Atavistic universe merely because the Source commonly possesses them.

A Tradition may define an explicit acquisition or expansion procedure inside the fixed Source. Such a procedure must itself be part of the Source definition when access is gained and must objectively state what new traits can enter the purchase universe, what event or input adds them, every cap and exclusion, and whether the addition is permanent. This expands the practitioner's legal purchases only through the written Source rule; it does not change the Source's identity or create unrestricted purchase-by-analogy.
